   would do so.  Would you then remove the book from the library's shelves?  
   I should hope that you would *not*.

Why should computer images, regardless of content, be treated differently?

It's the *public use* (if any) of this material that should concern us, 
NOT the material itself.  The fact that Waterloo has traditionally provided 
these materials to its community is an important point; despite your asser-
tions to the contrary, content-based actions of the type you propose are, 
indeed, censorship.

