I did a paper on this some time ago, and I think I reached a slightly
different conclusion.  While being polite is always a good policy, in
many newsgroups/mailing lists good manners and nice thoughs are foreign,
and the community encourages a loud, often obnoxious approach.  If one
doesn't follow the rules of the group, than that person may not
communicate effectively.  So instead of urging people to be nice, I'd
urge them to examine the rules of the community, and act accordingly
(remembering that different groups follow different practices.. 

