child protection in many jurisdictions, including Canada. People who 
point out that this exposes people such as system administrators to
risks (imprisonment, infamy, and a criminal record come to mind) they
never consented to take simply get dismissed as "hysteroids". For some
people, apparently, the freedom of the net amounts to complete license.

In their minds, the temporary immunity the network provides from laws
on copyright and child pornography gets equated with genuine freedom.
Well, we see the natural result in Ms. Prevost-Derbecker's case. She
would not have the ammunition to make the assault on the net she does
if someone had not provided it by (apparently) posting a highly
objectionable picture. 

